SUMMARY:CFA Society New York Lunch & Learn Series
DESCRIPTION:Overview\n \n\nFiera Capital is hosting the Fiera Comox Natural Capital Luncheon in partnership with CFA Society of New York\, covering key benefits of Natural Capital\, opportunities\, and risks. \n\n \n\nSarah Gal and Ben Lee\, Senior Principals at Fiera Comox\, will provide meaningful insights on the role of Agriculture & Sustainable Timberland asset classes in institutional portfolios and their growing relevance in today’s investment landscape. \n\nAttendees can expect a practical\, educational discussion on the investment case for natural capital\, its diversification potential\, and its evolving role within diversified portfolios. \n \n\n\n$115.2B(1)\nmulti-asset boutique investment firm\n\n\nOne of the largest\nopen-ended farmland funds globally(2)\n\n\nFiera Comox is the specialized natural capital GP within Fiera Capital’s $115.2B(1) multi-asset boutique investment firm. Fiera Comox Agriculture is one of the largest open-ended farmland funds globally(2) and has historically outperformed the NCREIF Farmland Index. In addition\, Fiera Comox Agriculture counts various U.S. tier 1 public pension funds as LPs and has broad support from prominent specialist consulting firms. \n \nThis Lunch & Learn will provide:\n\n1\nA deep dive into the potential benefits and opportunities of investing in Agriculture and Sustainable Timberland\n2\nCase studies highlighting the characteristics and performance drivers of these asset classes; and\n3\nThe opportunities and risks investors should consider.\n\n\nFeatured Speakers:\n\n\nSarah Gal \nSenior Principal\, Agriculture — Fiera Comox \nSarah has over a decade of experience in the institutional and direct agriculture industry. Prior to Fiera Comox\, Sarah held senior consulting roles at both Callan and Aon Hewitt. Most recently\, Sarah was a Senior Vice President\, Real Assets at Callan\, a leading institutional investment consulting firm\, where she was responsible for the firm’s farmland investment research. In this role\, she also worked with clients on real assets strategic planning\, investment research\, and asset class education. \nIn addition to her institutional experience in farmland\, Sarah has direct agriculture experience having managed a large dairy heifer growing operation for a dairy and cropping farm in Wisconsin. \nSarah holds a Bachelor of Science\, College of Agriculture with a concentration in Food Animal Science from the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign. \n\n\n\n\nBen Lee \nSenior Principal\, Timberland — Fiera Comox \nBen has a leading role in the sourcing\, due diligence and execution of new investment opportunities for the portfolio. Additionally\, Ben is actively involved in the management of assets across the portfolio and provides strategic oversight for portfolio companies. Ben has broad executive experience in the timberland and resource development industry. \nHe was most recently SVP\, Corporate Development & General Counsel for Mosaic Forest Management (“Mosaic”)\, Canada’s leading timberland manager with 585\,000 hectares (1.45 million acres) of privately owned forest\, where he was an executive for 9 years and led the pursuit of strategic growth opportunities for Mosaic (including M&A and non-timber opportunities) while overseeing the legal and governance functions. Ben played a leading role in the 2018 multi-billion transaction that brought together Island Timberlands and TimberWest to create Mosaic. He also played an integral part of the development\, launch and marketing of the largest nature-based carbon credit project in Canada. \nPrior to that\, he spent over 4 years at Goldcorp Inc. (TSX / NYSE) in a senior legal role\, where he led and managed the successful execution of over $12B in acquisition\, disposition\, joint venture and financing transactions. Before that\, he worked for over 5 years in the M&A / Securities Law Group of Fasken LLP\, a Canadian national law firm. \nIn 2019\, Ben was named 2019 Western Canada General Counsel “Dealmaker of the Year” for his integral role in the multi-billion-dollar transaction that brought together Island Timberlands and TimberWest to create Mosaic. In 2018\, Ben was named one of LEXPERT Canada’s “Top Under 40 Rising Stars”. \nBen holds a common law degree (LLB) from the University of Ottawa\, and Bachelor of Arts (political science) from McGill University. \n\n\n\nSponsor:
URL:https://cfany.org/event/cfa-society-new-york-lunch-learn-series-18/
LOCATION:CFA Society New York\, 1540 Broadway\, New York City\, NY\, 10036\, United States
