SUMMARY:CFA Society New York Lunch & Learn Series
DESCRIPTION:OverviewJoin us for a complimentary Lunch and Learn Session featuring a presenter and conversation on a range of topics. \n\n\nThis week\, our speaker will address \nMulti-Asset Credit: Navigating Today’s Credit Opportunity Set \nThe Lunch & Learn will provide an overview of the evolving multi-asset credit landscape and the different ways investors can access opportunities across high yield\, bank loans\, and structured credit\, exploring how investors can enhance returns and manage risk by more tactically allocating across a broader opportunity set in credit. The session will provide an update on how the liquid credit markets have drastically changed in the recent years and why investors need to revisit them now. We will discuss the spectrum of MAC approaches\, from more traditional liquid strategies to diversified\, opportunistic\, and public-private solutions\, and the portfolio considerations associated with each. \nWe will also share our current perspective on credit markets\, highlighting where we see relative value today and how a flexible\, cross-asset approach can help investors navigate changing market conditions and identify opportunities across the capital structure. Attendees will also gain insights into the benefits of incorporating European credit into portfolios\, where it can offer valuable diversification\, potential downside protection\, and relative value opportunities versus US markets. \n\nFeatured Speakers:\n\n\nJim Fitzpatrick \nCIO\, North America & Head of Global Loans — CQS Investment Management \nJames (Jim) Fitzpatrick is CIO North America and Head of Global Loans. Jim leads the dedicated loans team\, with portfolio managers and analysts based in both London and New York. He is responsible for managing the firm’s loan mandates\, including those within a variety of multi-asset credit funds and collateralized loan obligations. \nPrior to joining CQS in August 2015\, Jim was a Portfolio Manager within the Senior Secured Loan Group at Invesco\, focusing on separately managed institutional accounts and commingled funds. His previous experience at Invesco also included serving as a Senior Credit Analyst specializing in healthcare\, housing\, and leisure investments. \nJim holds a Bachelor of Science in Business from Wake Forest University. \n\n\n\n\nMark McKeown\, CFA \nHead of US Liquid Distribution — Manulife | CQS Investment Management \nMr. McKeown joined Manulife CQS in 2026 to lead US distribution efforts for the flagship Multi Asset Credit strategy and other liquid credit solutions. Prior to joining the firm\, he was Managing Principal and Head of Fixed Income Research at Meketa\, where he led the Fixed Income Public Markets Research Team and served as a Research Consultant to institutional clients utilizing his multi-asset credit expertise in structuring bond portfolios. \nHis prior experience includes corporate credit research analyst roles at hedge funds and allocator roles at family offices. Earlier in his career\, he worked as an Equity Research Analyst at Morgan Stanley. \nMark holds a Bachelor of Science in Finance from Providence College and is a Chartered Financial Analyst® charterholder. \n\n\n\nSponsor:
URL:https://cfany.org/event/cfa-society-new-york-lunch-learn-series-17/
LOCATION:CFA Society New York\, 1540 Broadway\, New York City\, NY\, 10036\, United States
