SUMMARY:The New Investment Playbook: Macro Resilience\, AI\, and the Future of Capital Markets
DESCRIPTION:OverviewThe investment landscape is undergoing a profound transformation. The Federal Reserve has entered a definitive new era of leadership\, and with this transition comes a fundamental recalibration of global macro strategy. At the same time\, heightened geopolitical uncertainty\, rapid advances in artificial intelligence\, and shifting capital flows are forcing investors to rethink traditional approaches to portfolio construction and risk management. \nCFA Society New York convenes a distinguished panel of investment leaders and market practitioners for a timely discussion on the forces shaping the next decade of capital markets. Moderated by Anthony Scaramucci\, Founder and Managing Partner of SkyBridge Capital\, this panel will explore how institutional investors are adapting to an evolving macroeconomic regime\, technological disruption\, and changing market structures. \nPanelists will examine the implications of the Federal Reserve’s new leadership\, the investment opportunities emerging from artificial intelligence\, the evolution of alternative investments\, and the challenges of preserving and generating alpha in a rapidly changing world. Through an engaging and interactive discussion\, attendees will gain actionable insights into the trends\, risks\, and opportunities expected to define the future of investing. \nIn keeping with CFA Society New York’s mission to deliver industry-leading content\, this event provides a premier forum for investment professionals to engage with leading voices at the intersection of macroeconomics\, innovation\, and capital markets \nAgenda5:30 PM | REGISTRATION \n\n6:00 PM | WELCOMING REMARKS \nStephan Puhlmann\, CFA\, CPA\, Director of Accounting and Finance\, SRCP \n\n6:05 PM | PANEL DISCUSSION \nMODERATOR \nAnthony Scaramucci\, Founder and Managing Partner\, SkyBridge Capital \nPANELIST \nJodie Gunzberg\, CFA\, Managing Partner\, InFi Strategies \nShahrukh Khan\, Editor in Chief\, Cash and Carried \nScott Treacy\, CFA\, Senior Associate\, Campion Capital \n\n7:15 PM | Q&A \n\n7:25 PM | CLOSING REMARKS \nAlton Crooks\, CFA\, Chair\, Business Management Group \n\n7:30 PM | NETWORKING RECEPTION
URL:https://cfany.org/event/the-new-investment-playbook-macro-resilience-ai-and-the-future-of-capital-markets/
LOCATION:Hybrid-CFA Society NY\, 1540 Broadway\, 10th Fl\, New York\, NY\, 10036\, United States
