SUMMARY:Leading with Feedback that Motivates Others
DESCRIPTION:OverviewEffective organizational leaders\, regardless of title\, provide specific and timely feedback to those they interact with to motivate them and to change behavior\, when necessary. During this workshop\, you will review and practice using a simple model for providing meaningful feedback that works\, regardless of whether feedback recipients are subordinates\, peers\, or superiors. \nIn turn\, developing your own skills and fostering a culture of feedback and improvement requires asking for and accepting feedback from others about your own performance. \nDuring this highly interactive workshop\, you will practice giving and receiving feedback that improves individual and team performance. \nLearning Outcomes: \n\nExplain the value of providing immediate feedback to motivate others\nDescribe and explain the impact of specific behaviors to a feedback recipient\nPractice providing and receiving on-the-spot feedback\nCreate a comfortable environment for providing non-judgmental feedback\n\nAgenda6:00 PM | WELCOMING REMARKS \nBob Wieczorek\, CFA\, Chief XP3RT\, Training and Consulting Consortium\, LLC \n\n6:10 PM | KENOTE SPEAKER \nLaura Smith Dunaief\, CPTM\, CLO and Founder\, CareerCraft \n\n7:10 PM | Q&A \n\n7:25 PM | CLOSING REMARKS \nBob Wieczorek\, CFA\, Chief XP3RT\, Training and Consulting Consortium\, LLC
